#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:433
msgid "Mentors module"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:436
#: includes/class-wpcpm-settings.php:572
msgid "Mentor status to sync"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:436
msgid "Only mentors holding this Airtable status get an account."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:440
#: includes/class-wpcpm-settings.php:573
#: includes/modules/class-wpcpm-mentors-dashboard.php:697
msgid "Currently mentoring"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:442
msgid "One status per line. Students holding any of these appear under \"Currently mentoring\" on their mentor's page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:447
#: includes/modules/class-wpcpm-mentors-dashboard.php:720
msgid "Past students"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:449
msgid "Statuses that mean mentoring has finished. These students appear in a separate, collapsed section. Leave empty to show only current students. A status listed in both boxes counts as current."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:454
msgid "When a mentor is no longer active"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:456
msgid "Remove the Mentor role and clear their student list"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:458
#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:513
msgid "Leave the role in place"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:459
msgid "The account itself is never deleted either way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:464
msgid "Invitation emails"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:466
msgid "Email each new mentor a password-reset link as their account is created"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:467
msgid "Off by default. A first sync creates around ninety accounts at once, so leave this off unless you mean to email all of them. Invitations are queued and sent a few at a time rather than all inside the sync, so a mail limit cannot swallow half of them unnoticed. You can also invite people one at a time from the Mentors and Students screens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:472
msgid "Automatic sync"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:474
msgid "Read Airtable on a schedule"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:483
msgid "Students and mentors every three hours, half an hour apart: the student rows carry what people are shown on their cards, and the students run is the expensive one, reading a WordPress.org profile per mentor, cached for twelve hours. A run already in progress is left to finish rather than restarted. Either can also be run by hand from the Students and Mentors screens. This switch governs the students, mentors and institutions syncs; the sponsors sync runs regardless."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:488
msgid "Mentor landing page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:490
msgid "Use the Mentor Report Card page as the mentor dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:491
msgid "Mentors go there when they log in and in place of the wp-admin Dashboard, and get a \"Mentor Report Card\" link in the toolbar. They keep access to their own profile screen, and a mentor who followed a link to somewhere specific still lands there instead. Administrators are unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:494
#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:525
msgid "The page is missing - re-activate the plugin to recreate it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:503
msgid "Students module"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:504
msgid "Uses the same status lists as the Mentors module above - a current student is anyone a mentor is currently mentoring."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:509
msgid "When a student leaves the program"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:511
msgid "Remove the Student role, so they lose access to Student-level content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:514
msgid "The account itself is never deleted either way, and their program details are kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:519
msgid "Student landing page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:521
msgid "Use the My Program page as the student dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:522
msgid "Students go there when they log in and in place of the wp-admin Dashboard, and get a \"My Program\" link in the toolbar. Same exceptions as for mentors: a requested destination wins, their own profile screen stays reachable, and anyone who can write posts is left alone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:541
msgid "Save settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:567
msgid "Institutions module"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:568
msgid "Institutions are the schools and universities whose students are on the program. Each has its own dashboard, its own people, and one Collaboration Agreement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:582
msgid "Applications from institutions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:584
msgid "Take applications through the form on this site"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:585
msgid "A public page anybody can post to. Every submission is stored for a program manager to read on the Institutions screen, and nothing is created until somebody approves it. While this is off the page shows one sentence saying applications are closed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:587
#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:720
msgid "No privacy policy page is set, so the form shows nothing to the public however this is switched. Publish one and choose it under Settings, Privacy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:591
#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:621
#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:724
msgid "The page is missing: re-activate the plugin to recreate it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:599
msgid "Enrollment lists from institutions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:601
msgid "Let an institution send a list of students to enroll"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:602
msgid "Adds an \"Enroll students\" section to the Institution Dashboard, where a school chooses the program and the term and then adds one student or sends a CSV. The list is read and checked against the program records, and the school sees what was understood before anything is created. While this is off the section does not appear at all."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: checks per hour, 2: rows per day.
#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:606
#, php-format
msgid "Ceilings per institution: %1$s checks an hour and %2$s students a day. Files are read and never stored."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:615
msgid "Institution landing page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:617
msgid "Use the Institution Dashboard page as the institution dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:618
msgid "Institution accounts go there when they log in and in place of the wp-admin Dashboard, and get an \"Institution Dashboard\" link in the toolbar. Same exceptions as for mentors and students."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:626
msgid "Create accounts automatically"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:628
msgid "Let the sync create the first account for a Confirmed institution"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:629
msgid "From the Contact Email Airtable holds, and only for a Confirmed institution whose agreement is recorded and that has never had a member. An address that already belongs to an account is left alone and named on the Institutions screen. With this off, accounts are created only when somebody presses the button there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:634
msgid "When an institution leaves the pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:636
msgid "Remove its people, so they lose access to its students"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:638
msgid "Leave their access in place"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:639
msgid "When Airtable moves an institution out of the stages the program treats as active. The accounts themselves are never deleted either way, and the agreement and the roster are kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:644
msgid "Agreement review"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:646
#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:670
msgid "days"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:647
msgid "How long a signed agreement may wait before the queue marks it overdue and the nightly digest names it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:652
msgid "Who reviews agreements"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:654
#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:678
#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:751
msgid "one@example.org, two@example.org"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:655
msgid "Addresses told when an agreement arrives and sent the overdue digest. Leave it empty and every program manager is written to, which reaches technical administrators as well; set it before the first real upload."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:660
#: includes/modules/class-wpcpm-administrators-cards.php:1316
#: includes/modules/class-wpcpm-institutions.php:4062
#: includes/modules/class-wpcpm-semester-report.php:307
msgid "Semester reports"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:662
msgid "Draft each institution's semester report when the semester ends"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:663
msgid "A daily job drafts a report for every finished semester and tells the program managers. Off, drafts are written only when a manager presses Draft now."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:668
msgid "Drafting grace"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:671
msgid "How long after a semester ends the job waits for students still in progress before drafting anyway. The draft says how many were still in progress."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:676
msgid "Who reviews reports"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:679
msgid "Addresses told when the job drafts a report. Leave it empty and every program manager is written to."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:684
msgid "The agreement wording"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:686
msgid "https://docs.google.com/document/d/..."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:687
msgid "The Google Doc the plugin's copy of the Collaboration Agreement was taken from, used by the Check against the Doc button. Held on this site rather than in the code, because the document is editable by anyone holding its link and the plugin's source is public. Google addresses only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:701
msgid "Sponsors module"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:702
msgid "Sponsors are the companies that fund mentors and offer their tools to students. Each has its own dashboard, its own people and its offer; a program manager creates each account one at a time from the Sponsors screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:715
msgid "Applications from sponsors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:717
msgid "Take sponsor applications through the form on this site"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:718
msgid "A public page anybody can post to. Every submission is stored for a program manager to read on the Sponsors screen and on the Administrator Dashboard, and nothing is created in Airtable until somebody approves it. While this is off the page shows one sentence saying applications are closed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:729
msgid "Sponsor home"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:731
msgid "Send sponsor accounts to the Sponsor Dashboard when they log in"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:732
msgid "Instead of the wp-admin Dashboard. Accounts that can also edit content or manage the program are left where WordPress sends them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:739
msgid "When a sponsor is no longer Approved"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:741
msgid "Keep its accounts as they are"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:743
msgid "Detach its accounts on the next sync"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:744
msgid "Airtable's Status is the record. Paused and Not Moving Forward sponsors keep their accounts by default, because a pause is often short; choose the other answer to have the sync detach them. Nothing is ever deleted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:749
msgid "Interest mail, when no manager is assigned"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:752
msgid "Addresses, comma-separated. A sponsor's interest is mailed to its assigned program manager; a sponsor with none is mailed here, or to every program manager when this is empty."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:757
msgid "Largest logo"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:759
msgid "KB"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:760
msgid "Applies to the logos the sync copies from Airtable and, later, to the ones sponsors upload. PNG, JPEG and WebP only; never SVG."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:765
#: includes/modules/class-wpcpm-sponsor-tools.php:309
#: includes/modules/class-wpcpm-students-dashboard.php:396
msgid "Tools from our sponsors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:767
msgid "Show the section on the Student Report Card"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:769
msgid "Show the section on the Mentor Report Card"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:770
msgid "Live offers, each with its claim button. A student always sees offers open to students; a mentor sees the offers whose sponsor opened them to mentors. The Administrator Dashboard shows every live offer whatever these say."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:774
msgid "Low-stock warning"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:776
msgid "codes left"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:777
msgid "When a pool of one-time codes falls below this many, the sponsor and its program manager are mailed once. The default for new offers; each offer can set its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:802
msgid "Two-factor authentication"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:807
msgid "Nobody is asked for a second factor, because the Two Factor plugin is not active on this site. Install and activate it, and the roles ticked below will be asked for a code as well as a password at their next sign-in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:812
msgid "An account in a ticked role is asked for a code as well as its password, from its next sign-in, with nothing to set up first: the code is emailed. Each person can then set up an authenticator app on their own profile screen, which is quicker and does not depend on their email. Untick everything to ask nobody."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:817
msgid "Roles that must use it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:825
msgid "Program managers (administrators)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:842
msgid "Students are left off by default: a student account holds that student's own work, there are hundreds of them, and there is nobody to unlock the ones who change phone. They can still turn it on for themselves."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:848
msgid "Where it stands"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: role name, 2: accounts covered, 3: accounts in the role, 4: accounts using an app.
#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:856
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s: %2$d of %3$d covered, %4$d using an authenticator app."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:868
msgid "Counted now, on this screen. An account that is covered but has no app is using emailed codes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:885
#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:895
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook-assistant.php:192
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook-assistant.php:237
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook-assistant.php:517
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook-assistant.php:556
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook-assistant.php:848
#: includes/tools/class-wpcpm-handbook.php:63
msgid "Need help?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:888
msgid "A question box for people on the program, answered from the WordPress documentation. The AI provider below does the searching, so nothing is stored on this site - and without a provider there is no answer at all. Each question, and the pages found for it, go to that company."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:897
msgid "Switch it on"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:898
msgid "Off means the question box answers nobody, the header button disappears and the page it lives on is unpublished. Nothing is deleted, so switching it back on restores all of it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:903
msgid "Where answers come from"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:904
msgid "The provider searches wordpress.org, make.wordpress.org, learn.wordpress.org and developer.wordpress.org itself. Nothing is copied to this site, so there is nothing to configure and nothing to refresh - and equally, no answer at all without a provider below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:922
msgid "Answer provider"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:924
msgid "Leave as \"None\" to keep everything on this site. Choosing a provider sends each question, and the extracts that match it, to that company."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:929
msgid "Provider API key"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:931
msgid "Stored in the database and never sent to the browser - leave blank to keep the current key. Get one free at aistudio.google.com for the Gemini provider."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:937
msgid "Model"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:939
msgid "Leave as gemini-flash-latest unless you have a reason not to. It is an alias that always points at the current Gemini Flash, so it cannot be retired out from under this site - which has already happened twice to specific version numbers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:943
msgid "Mentors and program managers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:944
msgid "Students and institutions as well"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpcpm-admin.php:945
